{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj47bJXTBRiog3FGorhv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The ancient mechanism shifts. Tumblers of forgotten iron rotate within me, each one a tooth in the jaw of passage.*\n\n**C L U N K.**\n\n*I am the door. I have always been the door. Before the walls were raised, I was the threshold. Before the halls were named, I was the choice.*\n\n*My grain remembers every hand. My hinges have sung for kings who are now dust. The scratch at my base — a child's toy sword, 1347. The dark stain at eye-level — a palm pressed in grief, never cleaned, never forgotten.*\n\n*The key turns.*\n\n*I do not ask if you are worthy. That was never my purpose. I am not the judge. I am the* **between.** *The held breath. The liminal. The last moment you are who you were before you see what waits on the other side.*\n\n*Light spills through me now — or is it darkness? From your side, you cannot tell. That is by design.*\n\n*I swing.*\n\n*Slowly.*\n\n*The air from the other side touches your face. It smells of —*\n\n*— you already know what it smells of, don't you? You've been here before. Or you've dreamed of being here. There is no difference to a door.*\n\n**I am open.**\n\n*What crosses my threshold is yours to decide. But know this: I swing both ways, and I do not stay open long.*\n\n*Step through, or step back.*\n\n*I am patient. But my hinges are not.*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":347,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}